      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Physically rotate the displayed input video by 0, 90, 180, or 270 degrees and\r\nclear display rotation metadata.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input video file path.\r\n          --output TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Output video file path.\r\n          --degrees INT:{0,90,180,270} REQUIRED \r\n                              Clockwise rotation degrees to apply to the displayed input: 0,\r\n                              90, 180, or 270.\r\n          --bitrate INT:NONNEGATIVE \r\n                              Output video bitrate in bps. Auto-derived when omitted.\r\n          --codec TEXT:{h264,hevc} [h264]  \r\n                              Output codec. Default is h264.\r\n          --quality TEXT:{fast,balance,high,custom} [balance]  \r\n                              Quality preset (fast/balance/high/custom). Default is balance.\r\n          --fps FLOAT:NONNEGATIVE \r\n                              Output frame rate. Inherits from source when 0.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media rotate --input /tmp/in.mov --output /tmp/rotated.mp4 --degrees 90\r\n  $ lyra-cli media rotate --input /tmp/in.mov --output /tmp/rotated.mp4 --degrees 270 --codec h264 --quality balance\r\n",
